issue_payload.body:
##### Description of change

Ensures that mouseover/pointerover events are always dispatched **after** mouseout/pointerout events.

Having these in essentially random ordering between components makes it unnecessarily complicated to react to hover state.

Consider this case:

```
let isMouseOver = false;

function onMouseOver() {
    isMouseOver = true;
}

function onMouseOut() {
    isMouseOver = false;
}

componentA.on('mouseover', onMouseOver);
componentB.on('mouseover', onMouseOver);

componentA.on('mouseout', onMouseOut);
componentB.on('mouseout', onMouseOut);
```

If componentA and componentB overlap, when you move from one component to the other in a certain direction with the cursor, you will receive a ``mouseover`` event **before** the other component dispatches the ``mouseout`` event, causing the above code to produce wrong results.

